        "entry_Pigqy9": {
          "type": "entry",
          "settings": {
            "full_width_enable": true,
            "title": "Troubleshooting",
            "text": "<p>Whilst we don't anticipate you having any issues with your hedge trimmer, here's some troubleshooting guidance if its not performing at its best.</p><p><strong> </strong></p><p><strong>01. Why isn't my hedge trimmer cutting as well as it did when it was new?</strong></p><p>This could be due to:</p><p>1. Too much friction due to the lack of lubrication. Lubricate the hedge trimmer blade with light machine oil.</p><p>2. The hedge trimmer blade is dirty. Clean the hedge trimmer blade.</p><p>3. The hedge trimmer blade is blunt. Sharpen following the guide in the maintenance section above or have the<br/>hedge trimmer blade replaced by a professional.</p><p>4. Your cutting technique is poor. Please refer to trimming section in the instruction manual.</p><p>5. The battery is not fully charged. Recharge the battery or it may be time to replace it.</p><p><strong> </strong></p><p><strong>02. My hedge trimmer blade feels warm after I've used it, why is that?</strong></p><p>This could be caused by one of three reasons:</p><p>1. The blades are blunt. Have the blades sharpened or sharpen the blades at home following the steps in the<br/>maintenance section above.</p><p>2. The blades are notched. Have the blades checked or replaced at a tool sharpening centre.</p><p>3. There is too much friction due to the lack of lubrication. Oil the blades with light machine oil.</p><p> </p><p><strong>03. My hedge trimmer has begun to switch off during use, what do I do?</strong></p><p>An internal contact may have knocked and become loose or the On/Off switch may have developed a fault. Please contact us to resolve using the contact form.</p>",
            "button_1_style": "white",
            "button_1_text": "",
            "button_1_url": "",
            "button_2_style": "white",
